          "domain": "craft-and-structure",
          "skill": "text-structure-and-purpose",
          "passage": "The following text is adapted from Lu Xun's 1918 short story \"A Madman's Diary.\" The narrator, who keeps a private journal, records the events of an evening walk through his old village.\n\nTonight there was no moon, and I knew that something was not right. I went out as far as the Zhao family gate, where their dog stood watching. He has watched me for many evenings now, and his eyes are not the eyes of a dog. The villagers I passed turned their heads as I went by — not all at once, which would have been ordinary, but one after another, as if a single instruction were making its way down the lane behind me. When I came home, I took down the old history and read by the lamp. Between the lines about benevolence and right conduct that fill every page, I have begun lately to make out two other words written so faintly that no one before me has thought to look. I will not set them down here; but I know now what the village has been eating.",
