          "passage": "Sociologist Patricia Hill Collins, a professor at the University of Maryland whose work centers on Black feminist thought, treats race, gender, and class not as separable identities to be tallied one after another but as a single intersecting structure. Earlier feminist accounts, she argues in *Black Feminist Thought* (1990), attended carefully to ______ they tended to set aside the simultaneous workings of race and class, leaving the standpoint from which Black women theorize largely uncharted.",
