          "domain": "expression-of-ideas",
          "skill": "transitions",
          "passage": "In Blindspot: Hidden Biases of Good People (2013), Harvard social psychologist Mahzarin R. Banaji reports a striking pattern: even people who hold sincere egalitarian beliefs about race and gender reliably show, on the Implicit Association Test, automatic associations linking certain social groups to negative attributes. The gap between what such respondents consciously affirm and what their reaction times reveal is wide and remarkably stable across replications. ______ Banaji concludes that good intentions alone cannot dismantle implicit bias; institutional safeguards — structured hiring rubrics, blind review, and routine audits of decisions — are needed to keep automatic associations from shaping consequential outcomes.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
